<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Adaptive launcher icon background for Clear Browser (logo v2).

  The source artwork is a finished round icon: a circular badge with a linear gradient
  from #211F26 to #4A4458 (at 315° / TL-to-BR) with the white "C" mark.
  Putting that whole image into the *foreground* layer would have the launcher mask it
  a second time, so the gradient is the background layer where the launcher's mask
  supplies the disc/squircle, and only the "C" mark is the foreground.

  ## Sizing the foreground

  The mark PNGs are cut from the artwork at a scale that preserves the artwork's
  own proportion of mark to disc:
    - Visible disc radius in launcher: 36dp (within 108dp viewport).
    - Artwork disc radius: 256px.
    - Artwork mark furthest pixel from center: 155.72px (radius ratio = 0.6083).
    - Resulting mark radius in launcher: 21.9dp (comfortably within 33dp safe circle).
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <gradient
        android:type="linear"
        android:angle="315"
        android:startColor="#211F26"
        android:endColor="#4A4458" />
</shape>
